# Stabilize line endings across platforms: every text file checks out as LF, so
# the Windows CRLF round-trip never shows up as diff noise. This repository is
# developed on Windows and consumed everywhere, and `scripts/check-readme-sync.mjs`
# compares fenced code blocks between the READMEs byte for byte — a line-ending
# difference would fail that gate for a reason that has nothing to do with the
# READMEs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets stay byte-identical.
*.tgz binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
